antatm (elevation) function

This function converts the geodetic elevation z in meters to atmospheric pressure p in hPa using the pressure-elevation relationships specifically for Antarctica.

Reference

Radok, Allison, Wendler, 1996. Atmospheric pressure over the interior of Antarctica. Antarctic Science 0 p. 209. 


input
	elevation – geodetic elevation in meters
output
	 pressure – atmospheric pressure in hPa

Example

elv_m = 1686; % meters. 
 
pressure = antatm(elv_m); % convert to atmospheric pressure in hPa


 
get_burial_age (X,samples,ztill,burialmask,P)

This function accepts the optimized 'X' structure and the till thickness structure 'ztill', obtain the sublimation parameters and set the inheritance parameters to zero, runs the forward model and add the predicted concentrations to the sampledata, finds the difference between the modeled and measured nuclide concentrations and caluclate the apparent burial age for a simple exposure and having steady-state erosion using the fsolver funtion.
 
This burial age is used as a constraint for the the forward model optimization as the optimized age cannot be older than the minimum burial age for any samples across all nuclide ratios.
 
The output is a burial age structure 'tb', which includes the following for each nuclide ratio: Be-10/Al-26, Be-10/Ne-21, Al-26/Ne-21

NaN is used for samples not used for burial calculations as indictated in burialmaks (= 0).

Input

	X – the parameter vector
X(1) sublimation rate m/Myr
X(2) erosion rate m/Myr
X(3) age Ma
X(4) inherited N10 (100000 atoms)
X(5) inherited N21 (Matoms)
X(6) inherited N26 (100000 atoms)
	samples – saved datasample structure
ztill – till thicknes structure: depth (.z) and mass depth (.dz)
P – the production rate structure (Pall)
Burialmask – n-element vector of zeroes and ones that tells which samples to consider for calculating burial age. 1 = use and 0 = don’t use

Output

tb.te_tb_N10_N26 = [te tb]
tb.te_tb_N10_N21 = [te tb]
tb.te_tb_N26_N21 = [te tb]

tb.ee_tb_N10_N26 = [ee tb] 
tb.ee_tb_N10_N21 = [ee tb] 
tb.ee_tb_N26_N21 = [ee tb] 

