get_misfit(data, samples, P, mask, nmask, DataDumpFlag, plotFlag) function

This function returns a single misfit value between modeled prediction and measured sample data, based on a goodness of fit calculation; ex. Chi-Square-like. The function is called upon within the objective_sublimation_model which includes all necessary parameters



Input
	data – data structure generated from sublimation_model_params.m
	samples – saved datasample structure
	P – the production rate structure (Pall)
mask – n-element vector of zeroes and ones that tells which samples to consider in calculating the misfit. 1 = use and 0 = don’t use
nmask – similar mask for nuclides to use.
dataDumpFlag – returns the predicted concentrations if requested (dataDumpFlag = 1) 
plotFlag – if omitted, plots predicted nuclide concentration. PlotFlag = 0 suppresses the plot and only provide the predicted nuclide concentration values

Output
	Out – Return single misfit value for use by optimizer
Out.nXp – if requested, returns the predicted cosmogenic nuclide concentrations of X element as a structure.

